<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13422" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποπίμπλημι</span></b> , later <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπο-πιμπλάω:</span></b>  poet. also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποπίπλημι</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπο-άω</span></b> :— <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fill up</i> a number, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς τετρακοσίας μυριάδας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.29
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>satisfy, fulfil,</i> in 
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποπλησθῆναι τὸν χρησμόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					8.96
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>satisfy, appease,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. αὐτοῦ τὸν θυμόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.129
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.68
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τὰς ἐπιθυμίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Grg.</u>
					492a
				</span></i>
			,al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>satisfy</i> an inquirer, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Cra.</u>
					413b
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
